# PRODUCTION — the real Supabase project. NEVER read by default; only
# scripts with an explicit "prod" opt-in (SUMMERICE_ENV=production) load
# this file, and each of those also runs a hard host guard first — see
# CLAUDE.md → "Environment files" and packages/db/guard-host.ts.
#
# Both connection strings below use the SAME pooler host
# (aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com), differing only by port. This is
# deliberate, not a shortcut: Supabase's plain "direct connection" host
# (db.<project-ref>.supabase.co) resolves to an IPv6-only address, which is
# unreachable from plenty of CI/serverless/sandboxed networks (confirmed
# directly against this project — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5). The pooler
# host is IPv4-reachable on both ports:
#
#   DATABASE_URL — transaction-mode pooler, port 6543. Runtime queries
#     (packages/db `dbPooled()`). Does not support prepared statements —
#     `dbPooled()` sets `prepare: false` to compensate; never remove that.
#
#   DIRECT_URL — session-mode pooler, port 5432. Migrations and one-off
#     scripts (`dbDirect()`, `drizzle-kit migrate`, `db:seed`). Supports the
#     multi-statement transactions a migration runs as, unlike transaction
#     mode. Get both exact strings from the Supabase dashboard — Project
#     Settings → Database → Connection string — rather than constructing
#     them by hand; the username embeds the project ref
#     (`postgres.<project-ref>`, not just `postgres`).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Browser + server. NEXT_PUBLIC_* is exposed to the client bundle by
# Next.js — fine here, the publishable key is designed to be public and
# Realtime fill counts are not secret (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §8).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<publishable-key>

# Server-only, once Supabase Auth is wired (a later session — see
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §7). Never exposed to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service-role-key>
